Logging and Audit Trail for Accountability
Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Configure auditd and rsyslog to capture system and database access events on Linux
Forward logs to a local Loki instance for centralized storage
Generate hourly cryptographic hashes of log files as tamper-evidence
Visualize access events in a Grafana dashboard
Compile an evidence pack suitable for an external compliance audit (GDPR Art. 5(2), GCC PDPL)
Prerequisites
Basic Linux command-line skills (systemctl, file permissions, cron)
Familiarity with SQL databases (any RDBMS)
Basic understanding of GDPR/PDPL accountability principles
Single Linux machine (Ubuntu 22.04 recommended) via Al Nafi Start Lab, with sudo access
Environment Setup
Your Al Nafi lab provides one Linux VM. Install required packages:

sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y auditd audispd-plugins rsyslog sqlite3 curl unzip gnupg
Install Loki and Grafana (open-source, local binaries — no cloud account needed):

# Loki
curl -O -L "https://github.com/grafana/loki/releases/latest/download/loki-linux-amd64.zip"
unzip loki-linux-amd64.zip && sudo mv loki-linux-amd64 /usr/local/bin/loki
chmod +x /usr/local/bin/loki

# Promtail (log shipper)
curl -O -L "https://github.com/grafana/loki/releases/latest/download/promtail-linux-amd64.zip"
unzip promtail-linux-amd64.zip && sudo mv promtail-linux-amd64 /usr/local/bin/promtail
chmod +x /usr/local/bin/promtail

# Grafana (APT repo)
sudo apt install -y software-properties-common
wget -q -O - https://apt.grafana.com/gpg.key | sudo gpg --dearmor -o /usr/share/keyrings/grafana.gpg
echo "deb [signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/grafana.gpg] https://apt.grafana.com stable main" | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/grafana.list
sudo apt update && sudo apt install -y grafana
Task 1: Configure auditd and rsyslog
Add audit rules to watch a sample "database" file representing personal data storage:
sudo mkdir -p /var/lib/appdata
echo "id,name,email" | sudo tee /var/lib/appdata/customers.csv
sudo auditctl -w /var/lib/appdata/customers.csv -p rwa -k pdpl_access
Persist the rule in /etc/audit/rules.d/audit.rules, then restart:
echo "-w /var/lib/appdata/customers.csv -p rwa -k pdpl_access" | sudo tee -a /etc/audit/rules.d/audit.rules
sudo systemctl restart auditd
