Troubleshooting
Promtail not shipping logs: check file permissions on log paths and Promtail's positions.yaml for stuck offsets
auditd rule lost on reboot: ensure rule is in /etc/audit/rules.d/audit.rules, not just added via auditctl
Grafana can't reach Loki: confirm Loki is bound to localhost:3100 and firewall allows local traffic
Conclusion
In this lab, you built an end-to-end accountability logging pipeline on a single Linux host: capturing file and database access events with auditd/rsyslog, centralizing them in Loki via Promtail, generating tamper-evident hourly hash ledgers, visualizing access patterns in Grafana, and assembling a structured evidence pack. These skills directly support demonstrating compliance with GDPR Article 5(2) accountability and GCC PDPL requirements, and are applicable to real-world Security Engineer and Compliance Analyst responsibilities, including audits aligned with ISO 27001 and CISA frameworks.
